course: dictionary
lesson: 10243
title: Tolerate and putting up with things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To tolerate something means to allow it, even though you do not like it, and not to stop it. «Bullying will not be tolerated» means the school will stop it. It will not be let carry on.
explain: Tolerate also means to put up with something unpleasant without complaining. You can tolerate noise, which means you can bear it. The example «put up with» means tolerate, so you can swap one phrase for the other in a sentence and it still makes sense.
explain: Plants and animals can tolerate things too. Some plants tolerate salt or drought, which means the salt or dry weather does not harm them. In citizenship lessons, tolerating other people's beliefs means respecting differences, even when you think differently.
fact: Tolerate is a verb: tolerate, tolerates, tolerated, tolerating.
fact: «Tolerate» means to allow something you do not like, without stopping it.
fact: «Put up with» means tolerate: to bear something unpleasant without complaining.
fact: «Zero tolerance» means that bad behaviour is not allowed at all.
fact: Some plants tolerate salt or drought, so they are not harmed by them.
exercise: What does «bullying will not be tolerated» mean? | It will be encouraged | *It will not be allowed | It will be a topic in a lesson | It will be written down in a book
exercise: «I can tolerate the noise of the traffic.» What does tolerate mean here? | Can stop it | Can hear it from far away | *Can bear it without complaining | Can enjoy it very much
exercise: Which word means to allow something you do not like, without stopping it? | hesitate | celebrate | decorate | *tolerate
test: A plant that tolerates frost is not harmed by it. What does tolerate mean? | *Is not harmed by | Is watered every day | Grows only in the sun | Is killed by
test: «Put up with» means tolerate. What does «put up with» mean? | *Bear something without complaining | Put away your toys | Put on a coat | Delay something until later
exam: What does «zero tolerance» mean in a school? | *Bad behaviour is not allowed at all | Pupils can choose their own rules | Teachers must tolerate every rule | Bad behaviour is allowed on Fridays
